From 36eb3b08e71506db6b96ff2daa879efdd15ef142 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Morris <jmorris@namei.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:22:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] mvp: CHERI proof of concept: the monitor and CHERI guests
 (work in progress)

beryllium-cheri's CHERI proof of concept (CHERI v0.9.3 under emulation,
QEMU 8.1 with the hypervisor extension), on a local branch of a clone,
never pushed:

- The monitor: henvcfg.CRE, a trap vector and resume tail that save and
  restore every guest register as a capability and switch ddc on every
  trap, hedeleg's cause 28, and the device tree passed to the guest as a
  capability in ca1 (beryllium-cheri's monitor-fix.patch, unchanged); the
  SBI 3.0 firmware contract (monitor-sbi30.patch, unchanged); and the
  injection helper moving sepcc and vstvecc whole, so that a denial's
  access fault reaches a CHERI guest's handler with its capabilities.
- The guests: tools/build-guest-cheri.sh builds every guest output as a
  CHERI program from the CHERI Alliance SDK and sources (outside the tool
  lock; guest.mk passes them, tools/make-control.py allows them): the
  init against CHERI musl, purecap; CHERI Alliance BusyBox with
  guest/busybox.config; CHERI Alliance Linux v7.1 with B6's and the MVP's
  fragments and guest/cheri-kernel.config, its exports trimmed to the
  management module's six imports (guest/cheri-ksyms.txt) to fit the
  kernel file budget; the module with a PCuABI ioctl argument; and the
  DTBs naming Zcherihybrid and Zcheripurecap. guest/pins.txt pins its
  outputs; two builds give the same bytes.
- The init's purecap port (guest/mvp-init.c, under
  __CHERI_PURE_CAPABILITY__): musl in place of nolibc, sigaction(), the
  ucontext's capability pc, the expected release 7.1.0, and
  clock_gettime by system call, since CHERI musl's vDSO call faults.
- tests/run-qemu.sh: OPENSBI_FW's SBI version is 3.0.

At this commit two-guests runs to RUN_COMPLETE with both inits' RESULT
pass on QEMU's plic machine; Beryllium's checkers are not yet adapted.

